# {{lb|en|baseball}} To touch a {{l|en|base|id=baseball}}, usually with a foot but sometimes with a hand.
# {{lb|en|by extension|colloquial|North America|usually|with "with"}} To [[meet]] or [[make contact with]] someone, usually to [[consult]], [[review]], [[visit]], or [[communicate]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Touch base''' with your boss before you start work to make sure you understand the project.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=A. Meredith Walters|title=Light in the Shadows|publisher=Simon and Schuster|isbn=9781476782300|page={{gbooks|ePGPAgAAQBAJ|55|touch|base}}
|passage=I had met with Dr. Todd right before dinner. He had wanted to '''touch base''' with me about my ongoing treatment.}}

